  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{x}, & -\\sqrt{e}<x<-1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}, & -1\\le x<1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{e}}^{1}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{e}}^{-1}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{1}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{e}}^{-1}x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{1}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{e}}^{-1}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x{|}_{-\\sqrt{e}}^{-1}+{\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =1-\\sqrt{e}+\\frac{1}{8}-\\frac{1}{8} \\\\  & =1-\\sqrt{e}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
